.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt EDQUOTA 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm edquota
.Nd edit disk quotas
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl u
.Op Fl p Ar proto-user
.Ar user ...
.Nm
.Fl g
.Op Fl p Ar proto-group
.Ar group ...
.Nm
.Op Fl u | g
.Fl t
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
writes the quotas of each
.Ar user
.Pq or group with Fl g
on every volume with quotas to a temporary file, runs the editor named
by
.Ev EDITOR
.Pq or Xr vi 1
on it, and stores the limits it reads back.
Each volume has two lines:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
/: 1K blocks in use: 12, limits (soft = 1000, hard = 2000)
	inodes in use: 5, limits (soft = 0, hard = 0)
.Ed
.Pp
Only the limits are read back; 0 means no limit.
A soft limit may be passed for the volume's grace period, a hard one
not at all.
The limits go to the kernel when quotas are on, and to the quota file.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl g
Groups.
.It Fl u
Users (the default).
.It Fl p Ar proto
Give each one the limits of
.Ar proto ,
without an editor.
.It Fl t
Edit the grace periods of the volumes instead:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
/: block grace period: 7 days, file grace period: 7 days
.Ed
.Pp
in days, hours, minutes or seconds.
They are read when quotas are turned on.
.El
.Pp
Only the super-user may run it; the super-user has no quotas.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr quota 1 ,
.Xr quotacheck 8 ,
.Xr quotaon 8 ,
.Xr repquota 8
.Sh HISTORY
Minkar's
.Nm
is its own.
